  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brenda’s historic core still shows the crumbling saloons, general store, and post office that once served early miners.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rvwest.com/article/tourism/enjoy_the_arizona_outback_in_brenda"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Prospectors first arrived in 1862, and a silver‑lead strike on the Ruby Silver claim in 1886 sparked a brief boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rvwest.com/article/tourism/enjoy_the_arizona_outback_in_brenda"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the silver ran out, the town was left with only a “worthless” copper deposit that failed to sustain the boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rvwest.com/article/tourism/enjoy_the_arizona_outback_in_brenda"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Camp Bouse, a top‑secret World War II tank‑testing base, sits just outside Brenda and draws history buffs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rvwest.com/article/tourism/enjoy_the_arizona_outback_in_brenda"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Brenda offers several RV parks that serve as a convenient home base for exploring the surrounding legends and historic sites.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.rvwest.com/article/tourism/enjoy_the_arizona_outback_in_brenda"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town is surrounded by public lands, making it a favorite spot for nature lovers and off‑road enthusiasts alike.",
